<https://opus-project.eu/letter/Smith1_letter_101> a opus:LetterManifestation,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:abstract "This letter from Henry Wotton to Sir Thomas Edmondes, dated May 18, 1607, provides a detailed account of the resolution of the Venetian conflict with the Papacy. Wotton outlines the specific terms of the agreement, which include the revocation of the Pope’s interdict, the conditional return of certain religious orders (excluding the Jesuits), and the extradition of two ecclesiastical prisoners to Rome at the request of the French King. He notes the strategic ambiguity in the language used by both sides, particularly regarding the Pope’s authority, hinting at unresolved tensions. Wotton also highlights the Venetian Senate’s decision to grant lifelong protection and pensions to the intellectual defenders of the Republic, emphasizing the ongoing ideological battle. He describes how the Cardinal de Joyeuse formally revoked the interdict under French auspices, yet Venice minimized any public recognition of this papal act, reinforcing its stance of maintaining full sovereignty. The letter concludes with Wotton’s reflection on the subtle diplomatic maneuvering and his expectation that tensions would persist, albeit in a less overt form." ;
    bibo:edition "Pearsall Smith 1907, pp. 485-488" ;
    skos:note "letter_39 in the old chart (Wotton_Jes_Letters)" ;
    opus:authorAsMarked "Henry Wotton" ;
    opus:dateAsMarked "18th of May, 1607. Style of the place." ;
    opus:destination [ opus:certainty "inferred" ;
            opus:value <https://opus-project.eu/place/place_10> ] ;
    opus:destinationAsMarked "Brussels" ;
    opus:incipit "Having formerly given your Lordship a general accompt" ;
    opus:originAsMarked "Venice" ;
    opus:recipient [ opus:certainty "certain" ;
            opus:value <https://opus-project.eu/person/person_241> ] ;
    opus:recipientAsMarked "Sir Thomas Edmondes" ;
    schema:author [ opus:certainty "certain" ;
            opus:value <https://opus-project.eu/person/person_110> ] ;
    schema:dateCreated "1607-05-18"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:inLanguage "English" ;
    schema:locationCreated [ opus:certainty "certain" ;
            opus:value <https://opus-project.eu/place/place_1> ] .

