<https://opus-project.eu/letter/Smith1_letter_106> a opus:LetterManifestation,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:abstract "This letter from Henry Wotton to Sir Thomas Edmondes discusses two key issues: the political-religious tensions in the Grisons and the conversion of Tobie Matthew to Catholicism. Wotton reports on the ongoing struggle between the Grisons and the Spanish, highlighting Count Fuentes’ attempt to frame the conflict as a religious persecution to rally Catholic allies. He also mentions the fear that Archduke Maximilian of Tyrol may intervene, exacerbating tensions. Additionally, Wotton expresses disappointment at the conversion of Tobie Matthew, son of the Archbishop of York, lamenting the potential influence of Jesuits in exploiting his apostasy. The letter reflects Wotton’s concern for the Protestant cause in Europe and his broader intelligence-gathering efforts." ;
    bibo:edition "Pearsall Smith 1907, pp. 492-494" ;
    skos:note "letter_40 in the old chart (Wotton_Jes_Letters)" ;
    opus:authorAsMarked "Henry Wotton" ;
    opus:dateAsMarked "3rd of August, 1607. Style of the place." ;
    opus:destination [ opus:certainty "inferred" ;
            opus:value <https://opus-project.eu/place/place_10> ] ;
    opus:destinationAsMarked "Brussels" ;
    opus:incipit "Your Lordship's of the 11th of July" ;
    opus:originAsMarked "Venice" ;
