<https://opus-project.eu/letter/Smith1_letter_131> a opus:LetterManifestation,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:abstract "This letter, dated from Venice in May (?), 1608, relays intelligence from Rome concerning Tyrone’s activities. According to the report, Tyrone—accompanied largely by the Primate of Ireland—visited various cardinals and ambassadors. From Cardinals Farnese and Mont’ Alto he received favorable words. In Rome, among a group dispatched from the English College (including Thomas Fitzharbert and John Sweete), he was noted for his interaction with English exiles. Notably, upon seeing Sir Anthony Standen, he is reputed to have declared that “it is better being poor in Rome than rich in prison in England.” Furthermore, the letter details two private audiences with the Pope, mentions his lodging in a palace alongside the Persian ambassador and Sir Anthony Sherly, and reports that the Pope intends to limit his board to twelve persons amid rising discontent. Rumors include a pension of ten thousand crowns per annum from the King of Spain for the support of the Irish, along with scattered personal observations regarding Tyrone’s wife. Overall, the letter interweaves documented diplomatic encounters with rumor, reflecting the intricate network of political, religious, and personal intrigues among exiled English and Irish figures in Rome." ;
    bibo:edition "Pearsall Smith 1907, pp. 541-543" ;
    skos:note "letter_25 in the old chart (Wotton_Jes_Letters)" ;
    opus:dateAsMarked "⟨Venice, May (?), 1608.⟩" ;
    opus:dateIsApproximate true ;
    opus:destination [ opus:certainty "inferred" ;
            opus:value <https://opus-project.eu/place/place_4> ] ;
    opus:destinationAsMarked "London" ;
    opus:incipit "Such particulars as I hear from Rome touching Tirone" ;
    opus:originAsMarked "Venice" ;
    opus:recipient [ opus:certainty "certain" ;
            opus:value <https://opus-project.eu/person/person_199> ] ;
    opus:recipientAsMarked "Earl of Salisbury" ;
    schema:author [ opus:certainty "inferred" ;
            opus:value <https://opus-project.eu/person/person_110> ] ;
    schema:dateCreated "1608-05"^^xsd:gYear ;
    schema:inLanguage "English" ;
    schema:locationCreated [ opus:certainty "inferred" ;
            opus:value <https://opus-project.eu/place/place_1> ] .

