<https://opus-project.eu/letter/Smith1_letter_189> a opus:LetterManifestation,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:abstract "Henry Wotton reports to the Earl of Salisbury about a dubious French informant, Claudio de’ Giuberti, who claims to have uncovered a plot against King James I in Rome. The informant, allegedly trained at the Papal Court, describes an Englishman seeking revenge for religious persecution, supposedly carrying a stiletto as proof of his intent. Wotton, skeptical of the informant’s credibility, confirms with the French ambassador that he was a known opportunist seeking financial reward. Additionally, Wotton discusses the trial and execution of Fra Fulgenzio Manfredi in Rome, noting that false accusations were made against him regarding correspondence with King James and the English ambassador. Wotton publicly refutes these charges, leading to a strong reaction in the Venetian Senate, reinforcing his role in defending England’s interests." ;
    bibo:edition "Pearsall Smith 1907, pp. 632-635" ;
    skos:note "letter_34 in the old chart (Wotton_Jes_Letters)" ;
    opus:authorAsMarked "Henry Wotton" ;
    opus:dateAsMarked "29th of October, 1610" ;
    opus:dateIsUncertain true ;
    opus:destination [ opus:certainty "inferred" ;
            opus:value <https://opus-project.eu/place/place_4> ] ;
    opus:destinationAsMarked "London" ;
    opus:incipit "Not long since a gentleman of some forty years" ;
    opus:originAsMarked "Venice" ;
    opus:recipient [ opus:certainty "certain" ;
            opus:value <https://opus-project.eu/person/person_199> ] ;
    opus:recipientAsMarked "Earl of Salisbury" ;
    schema:author [ opus:certainty "certain" ;
            opus:value <https://opus-project.eu/person/person_110> ] ;
    schema:dateCreated "1610-10-29"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:inLanguage "English" ;
    schema:locationCreated [ opus:certainty "certain" ;
            opus:value <https://opus-project.eu/place/place_1> ] .

<https://opus-project.eu/letter/Smith1_letter_19> a opus:LetterManifestation,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:abstract "In this letter, dated April 21, 1591, from Vienna, Henry Wotton updates Lord Zouche on various matters, including his return of a book of arms and descents and his difficulties obtaining an architectural model. He describes his failed attempt to secure a drawing of a Lusthaus (pleasure house) from a master architect, who had lent the model to an Italian. Wotton suspects that the architect still possesses it but requires a bribe. Additionally, he reports a discovered plot in Graz to massacre Lutherans, possibly orchestrated by Rome, and how it was foiled when a messenger mistakenly delivered incriminating documents to the wrong Chapel Master. He also provides a colorful account of an Englishman in Vienna, Abraham Miller, whose misadventures reflect both personal folly and the broader tensions between the English and the Austrians regarding employment opportunities." ;
    dcterms:subject <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/codenames>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/conspiracy>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/international_politics>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/lutherans>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/papacy>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/protestantism>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/religion> ;
    bibo:edition "Pearsall Smith 1907, pp. 323-325" ;
    skos:note "letter_57 in the old chart (Wotton_Jes_Letters)" ;
    opus:authorAsMarked "Henry Wotton" ;
    opus:dateAsMarked "21st of April, CLↃLↃXCI. " ;
    opus:hasNameAppearance [ opus:nameAsUsed "Archduke" ;
            opus:person <https://opus-project.eu/person/person_24> ],
        [ opus:nameAsUsed "the Emperor" ;
            opus:person <https://opus-project.eu/person/person_64> ],
        [ opus:nameAsUsed "Jesuit College Chapel Master" ;
            opus:person <https://opus-project.eu/person/person_139> ],
        [ opus:nameAsUsed "brothers of the house of Austria" ;
            opus:person <https://opus-project.eu/person/person_13> ],
        [ opus:nameAsUsed "D. Blotius" ;
            opus:person <https://opus-project.eu/person/person_66> ],
        [ opus:nameAsUsed "Abraham Miller" ;
