<https://opus-project.eu/letter/Smith1_letter_21> a opus:LetterManifestation,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:abstract "This letter from Wotton to Lord Zouche reports on Wotton’s personal illness, the visit of Archduke Maximilian to Rome, and the broader political maneuvering surrounding his visit. Wotton describes Maximilian’s humble attire upon his arrival in Rome, emphasizing his religious piety and the clandestine nature of his interactions with Jesuits and Cardinal Madrutz. The Pope, having recently staged an illness due to a prior political incident, was hesitant to meet the Archduke but eventually did so. There is speculation about the purpose of Maximilian’s visit. Some believed it was to prevent the marriage between the King of Poland (Sigismund III) and a daughter of Austria, but others dismissed this theory in favor of the idea that Maximilian sought Papal intervention to pressure the Emperor into abdicating either the Roman or Hungarian crown in his favor. The letter also notes that the Pope presented Maximilian with a religious relic and a gold medaglia, laden with indulgences—a gesture Wotton dismisses with sarcasm. On a personal note, Wotton discusses his continued residence in Florence at the house of Bacchio Boni, his financial concerns, and his likely stay in Italy over the summer. The letter closes with a request to remain informed of any relevant political affairs." ;
    dcterms:subject <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/international_politics>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/papacy>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/political_marriage>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/politics>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/private_matters>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/religion> ;
    bibo:edition "Pearsall Smith 1907, pp. 333-335" ;
    skos:note "letter_58 in the old chart (Wotton_Jes_Letters)" ;
    opus:authorAsMarked "Henry Wotton" ;
    opus:dateAsMarked "⟨May 29, 1592.⟩" ;
    opus:dateIsInferred true ;
    opus:hasNameAppearance [ opus:nameAsUsed "King of Poland" ;
            opus:person <https://opus-project.eu/person/person_209> ],
