<https://opus-project.eu/letter/Smith1_letter_27> a opus:LetterManifestation,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:abstract "This letter, written on August 29th 1592, presents a report by Henry Wotton to Baron Edward La Zouche, detailing the recent affairs in Europe, starting with the political marriage of Leonora Ursina and rumours surrounding it. The author speaks also of the situation in Rome, where Pope has executed a few people for sodomy and a gruesome murder was committed. Two new bans (bandi) are discussed, one against Jews and another against Spanish courtesans. The letter also relates the movements of several European officials, Baron of Bernstein and John de Taxis." ;
    dcterms:subject <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/courtesans>,
