<https://opus-project.eu/letter/Smith1_letter_28> a opus:LetterManifestation,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:abstract "This letter, written on September 6th 1592, presents a report by Henry Wotton to Baron Edward La Zouche, detailing the recent affairs in Italy, The letter narrates the aftermath of a recent battle near Mantua, mentions a plague in Vienna, and briefly touches upon the topic of the correspondence of John de Taxis, aka Thomas Darcy, 3rd Lord of Chiche. The author speaks about the state of his mission in Italy, currently awaiting further orders and planning to depart to France after six months and stay there for a year. " ;
    dcterms:subject <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/battle>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/diplomacy>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/international_politics>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/plague>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/politics>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/war> ;
