<https://opus-project.eu/letter/Smith1_letter_55> a opus:LetterManifestation,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:abstract "In this letter, Henry Wotton informs Robert Cecil, Viscount Cranborne, of the ongoing deliberations in Venice regarding maritime piracy and the English response to Venetian naval interference. He discusses the case of Nicolo Balbi, a Venetian accused of murdering an English merchant, Nicholas Pardoe, and emphasizes his role as both an accuser and a negotiator in securing justice for the victim. Wotton details his exchanges with Advocate Finetti, Balbi’s legal defender, noting his attempts to persuade Balbi to confess and deliver the stolen money and documents. He stresses his diplomatic balancing act—ensuring that Venice does not perceive English intervention as an overreach while still maintaining England’s demand for justice. Wotton expresses confidence that Balbi will not escape punishment unless unforeseen circumstances intervene. He also briefly mentions that the papal conclave remains unresolved and that Robert Parsons, the prominent English Jesuit, has returned to Rome, hinting at further intelligence to be conveyed to the English crown." ;
    dcterms:subject <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/cipher>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/diplomacy>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/international_politics>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/murder>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/papacy>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/papal_conclave>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/piracy>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/trial> ;
    bibo:edition "Pearsall Smith 1907, pp. 395-397" ;
    skos:note "letter_4 in the old chart (Wotton_Jes_Letters)" ;
    opus:dateAsMarked "3th of May, 1605." ;
    opus:dateIsUncertain true ;
    opus:destination [ opus:certainty "inferred" ;
            opus:value <https://opus-project.eu/place/place_4> ] ;
    opus:destinationAsMarked "London" ;
    opus:hasNameAppearance [ opus:nameAsUsed "Advocate Finetti" ;
            opus:person <https://opus-project.eu/person/person_71> ],
        [ opus:nameAsUsed "Parsons" ;
            opus:person <https://opus-project.eu/person/person_200> ],
        [ opus:nameAsUsed "his Majesty" ;
            opus:person <https://opus-project.eu/person/person_119> ],
        [ opus:nameAsUsed "Parde" ;
            opus:person <https://opus-project.eu/person/person_158> ],
