<https://opus-project.eu/letter/Smith1_letter_56> a opus:LetterManifestation,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:abstract "This letter, written by Henry Wotton to Viscount Cranborne in May 1605 from Venice, discusses intelligence matters related to the political situation in Italy and Spain. Wotton informs Cranborne about the uncertain status of the papal election following the death of Clement VIII, the return of the Jesuit Robert Parsons to Rome, and the broader Spanish influence in the region. He describes his deployment of two agents—Rowland Woodward, sent to Milan, and George Rooke, sent to Naples—both involved in espionage regarding Spanish military and political maneuvers. Wotton expresses concern about Parsons’ activities and their implications for English interests." ;
    dcterms:subject <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/catholicism>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/conspiracy>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/espionage>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/international_politics>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/papists>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/protestantism>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/religion> ;
