<https://opus-project.eu/letter/Smith1_letter_58> a opus:LetterManifestation,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:abstract "In this letter, dated August 18, 1605, Henry Wotton writes to the Earl of Salisbury about reports of Catholic agitation in Wales and broader concerns regarding the influence of Rome on English subjects. He warns that the Catholic party is growing and expresses anxiety over the conversion efforts of Jesuits, seminary priests, and other Catholic missionaries. Wotton frames this religious activity as a form of corruption, suggesting that the Pope and Jesuits are engaged in a systematic effort to undermine England’s Protestant stability. He contrasts past papal approaches, particularly those of Sixtus V and Clement VIII, arguing that the latter encouraged religious infiltration rather than violent persecution. The letter reflects a conspiratorial tone, portraying Catholic influence as a covert and organized threat. Wotton also comments on the diplomatic maneuvers of Pope Paul V, particularly his relationship with King James I, and mentions figures such as Monsignor Paulino, who appears to be maneuvering within the papal court. The letter exemplifies how early modern diplomatic correspondence blended intelligence gathering with political and religious anxieties, demonstrating both real geopolitical concerns and conspiratorial thinking." ;
    dcterms:subject <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/cardinalship>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/catholicism>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/conspiracy>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/crime>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/embassy>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/espionage>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/execution>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/international_politics>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/papacy>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/papists>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/protestantism>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/religion>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/religious_conversion> ;
    bibo:edition "Pearsall Smith 1907, pp. 404-410" ;
    skos:note "letter_5 in the old chart (Wotton_Jes_Letters)" ;
    opus:dateAsMarked "18 of August, 1605." ;
    opus:dateIsUncertain true ;
