<https://opus-project.eu/letter/Smith1_letter_67> a opus:LetterManifestation,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:abstract "In this letter, Henry Wotton writes to the Earl of Salisbury, excusing himself for the shortness of his letter (caused by his illness), and briefly detailing the current situation in Venice, following the Papal interdict and its rejection by all the Venetian authorities. Wotton finishes by mentioning a few of his other messengers, which have been recently sent with other dispatches. " ;
