<https://opus-project.eu/letter/Smith1_letter_69> a opus:LetterManifestation,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:abstract "Wotton reports to the Earl of Salisbury on the state of affairs in Italy following the Papal interdict of 1606, where the differences between the Pope and Venice have grown substancially. He tells of the departure  of Papal Nuncio from Venice as well as expulsion of the Venetian ambassador from Rome and mentions his two visits to Venice's Full College, which allowed him to learn of these events and judge the  actions of the Venetian State as prudent and magnificent. Finally, he expresses his hopes that this state of affairs will continue to restrict Church's control over the State matters, seeing the current situation as a confirmation of God's influence in Italy. " ;
    dcterms:subject <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/diplomacy>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/embassy>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/international_politics>,
