<https://opus-project.eu/letter/Smith1_letter_70> a opus:LetterManifestation,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:abstract "Wotton reports on the Feast of Corpus Christi in Venice, a grand event with extensive religious imagery, which he interprets as a demonstration of Venetian defiance against the Pope’s interdict. He describes the Benedictine monks’ clever workaround to avoid papal authority by using a locked chest to prevent the reception of prohibitory orders from Rome. He also notes the ongoing legal process against the Jesuits before the Council of Ten. Wotton expresses optimism that Venice may draw closer to England, not just politically but also in matters of religion. To further this, he has arranged for an Italian Protestant preacher to be sent from Geneva. The letter concludes with Wotton requesting further financial support, emphasizing that his secret intelligence efforts (particularly intercepting Jesuit communications) require substantial funding." ;
    dcterms:subject <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/celebration>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/cipher>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/conspiracy>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/espionage>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/financial_problems>,
