<https://opus-project.eu/letter/Smith1_letter_75> a opus:LetterManifestation,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:abstract "Henry Wotton writes to the Earl of Salisbury, informing him of a dispatch which the Venice's Pien Collegio (Full College) intends to send to the Venetian ambassador (Zorzi Giustinian) in England. He describes the letter's contents, including: thanks to king James I for his reception of the ambassador as well as his general support towards Venice, information about the ongoing troubles with the Pope (who has started to engage in military actions) following the Venetian interdict, the support that the Spanish King has shown to the Pope, as well as Venice's declaration to continue defending their independence. Wotton relates how he has communicated the king's positive attitude towards Venice and expresses his joy derived from his contribution to maintaining this diplomatic bond. " ;
    dcterms:subject <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/diplomacy>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/embassy>,
        <https://opus-project.eu/keyword/international_politics>,
