<https://opus-project.eu/letter/Smith1_letter_78> a opus:LetterManifestation,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:abstract "Henry Wotton writes to king James I to thank him for a recently received letter, in which the monarch has conveyed approval towards his ambassador in Venice. Emphasizing his gratitude and the king's own virtues, Wotton shows his humble allegiance, ending the letter with the prayer for the long preservation of his Lord and Sovereign. " ;
