<https://opus-project.eu/letter/Smith1_letter_79> a opus:LetterManifestation,
        schema:CreativeWork ;
    dcterms:abstract "In this letter, Henry Wotton writes to the Earl of Salisbury, informing him of the rumours in Venice concerning the leagues which are supposedly being formed by certain European countries. Kings of England and Denmark are believed to be seeking an alliance with Venice, the States, Protestant German Princes and possibly the French king, as well as Protestants from France, Poland and Hungary. Other rumours, which Wotton deems somewhat credible, tell of Pope secretly attempting to forge a league with Spain, Emperor Rudolf II and the Italian Princes. Wotton claims that this ongoing process is the reason why the situation in Italy hasn't yet fully escalated to war, as the Pope hasn't yet secured all of his desired alliances. " ;
